EMAIL 3: HOW TO USE AURA EFFECTIVELY

Subject: 11 things to ask Aura when your brain is doing too much

Hi love,

One of the easiest ways to use Aura is to stop waiting for the perfect question.

Most women think they need to arrive with clarity, but clarity usually comes after the nervous system feels supported enough to stop performing. When you are overwhelmed, your brain will try to solve everything by thinking harder, analysing more, replaying the same situation, or searching for certainty.

But your body often needs regulation before your mind can access perspective.

So when you open Aura and do not know where to begin, start with what feels most emotionally present.

You can ask Miss Aura:

* I feel anxious and I don’t know why. Help me understand what may be happening in my nervous system.

* I am overthinking something and I need to regulate before I react.

* I feel blocked around money. Help me find the subconscious belief underneath this.

* I feel unsafe being visible, successful, or fully seen.

* I keep sabotaging something I deeply want. Help me understand the emotional pattern.

* Create an EFT tapping script for the emotion I am feeling right now.

* Give me a journaling prompt for the pattern I keep repeating.

* Help me move from scarcity into a more regulated state of receiving.

* Guide me through a visualisation for the version of me I am becoming.

* Help me understand why I feel guilty when I rest or receive support.

* Help me regulate before I make a decision from fear.

Inside Aura, you can use:

* Miss Aura for personalised emotional, manifestation, and subconscious support

* Journaling for clarity, release, and pattern recognition

* EFT tapping for specific fears, beliefs, triggers, and emotional blocks

* Nervous system practices for regulation and grounding

* Visualisations for identity work, receiving, self-concept, and manifestation

* Masterclasses and resources that are updated frequently for deeper learning

A simple rhythm we recommend is this:

* Use Aura daily for one honest check-in.

* Use EFT when something feels charged in the body.

* Use journaling when your mind feels full.

* Use Miss Aura when you need personalised reflection.

* Use masterclasses when you want deeper education.

* Use visualisations when you want to practise becoming the version of you that already has the life you are calling in.

The goal is not to use everything at once. The goal is to build a relationship with your inner world where you know how to support yourself in the moments that usually pull you out of alignment.

This matters because your RAS, the part of your brain that filters what feels relevant, starts noticing new evidence when your nervous system can actually tolerate the new identity you are choosing. If your body still feels unsafe receiving, being seen, earning more, resting, or being loved well, your brain may keep filtering reality through old emotional patterns.

Aura helps you work with both.

The mind that wants more.

And the body that needs to feel safe enough to hold more.

If anything feels confusing while using Aura, please reply to this email. We are happy to guide you, and we would genuinely love to hear what is working, what feels supportive, and what you would like us to improve.

With love,
Team Aura





EMAIL 4: FOUNDER NOTE

Subject: 7 reasons manifestation feels hard even when you’re doing everything right

Hi love,

There is a pattern I kept seeing in ambitious, emotionally aware, intelligent women.

They were not lazy. They were not unmotivated. They were not lacking desire, discipline, vision, or self-awareness.

In fact, most of them were doing too much.

They were journaling, visualising, learning, healing, working, achieving, reflecting, holding their relationships together, trying to regulate, trying to manifest, trying to become magnetic, and still quietly wondering why certain patterns kept repeating.

This is one of the reasons Aura exists.

Because manifestation does not work deeply when the body still feels unsafe receiving what the mind says it wants.

Your nervous system responds to emotional memory, not just beautiful affirmations. If your body has learned that visibility brings judgment, money brings pressure, love brings disappointment, rest brings guilt, or success makes you unsafe, then a part of you may keep resisting the very life you are consciously calling in.

Here are a few reasons manifestation can feel hard even when you are doing the work:

* Your body may still associate receiving with responsibility, pressure, or loss of control.

* Your subconscious may be protecting you from visibility because being seen once felt unsafe.

* Your nervous system may be addicted to urgency because calm feels unfamiliar.

* Your identity may still be organised around proving, performing, or earning love.

* Your mind may want expansion, but your body may still be bracing for disappointment.

* You may be trying to manifest from scarcity instead of regulated desire.

* You may be consuming spiritual information without creating nervous system safety.

* Your self-concept may have changed mentally, but your body may not yet experience the new identity as emotionally safe.

* Your brain’s RAS may still be filtering for old evidence because the new reality has not become familiar enough in your system.

I wanted Aura to become a space where women could work with all of this in a way that feels intelligent, feminine, grounded, and deeply supportive.

A space where you can speak honestly to Miss Aura, use EFT when a belief feels charged, journal through the emotional pattern underneath your reaction, regulate your body before making decisions, practise visualisations from a safer internal state, and keep learning through masterclasses and resources that support your becoming.

This is where neuroscience, manifestation, and emotional regulation meet. Not as separate practices, but as one integrated way of becoming the woman who can hold what she is asking for.

Not because you are broken.

Because your patterns make sense when you understand what your system has been trying to protect.

Use Aura for the parts of you that feel powerful, and use it for the parts of you that feel embarrassed, jealous, tired, insecure, avoidant, ambitious, emotional, or afraid of wanting more.

The more truthfully you meet yourself, the more deeply this work can support you.

Regulate and become.

With love,
Sanaya




EMAIL 5: TRIAL ENDING EMAIL

Subject: The mistake most women make after their first nervous system shift

Hi love,

One of the biggest mistakes women make after experiencing a small emotional shift is assuming the work is complete.

You regulate once and feel lighter, so you think you are done. You journal once and feel clear, so you stop returning. You do one EFT practice and feel the charge reduce, so you forget that the body learns through repetition, not intensity.

The nervous system does not rewire because something helped once. It begins to change when safety becomes familiar enough to return to.

This is why consistency matters, but not in the rigid, productivity-obsessed way we are usually taught.

Consistency in inner work can look like:

* Checking in with yourself before you spiral

* Using EFT when a money fear or relationship trigger feels charged

* Journaling inside Aura when your thoughts feel tangled

* Asking Miss Aura to help you understand a repeating emotional pattern

* Using a regulation practice before making a decision from fear

* Watching a masterclass when you want deeper understanding

* Returning to visualisation when your body feels safe enough to hold a new identity

* Noticing when your dopamine system is craving urgency, scrolling, drama, or overstimulation instead of stillness

* Practising the same new emotional state often enough for your brain to register it as familiar

You do not need to use everything every day. You do not need to become the perfect healing girl. You do not need to turn your inner work into another performance.

You only need to return often enough for your body to learn that this new way of being is safe.

This is where neuroplasticity becomes practical. Your brain does not build new pathways through one powerful moment alone. It builds them through repeated emotional experiences, repeated regulation, repeated self-concept reinforcement, and repeated evidence that the new version of you is safe to become.

Your 15-day complimentary trial is coming to an end soon, and we wanted to remind you gently that Aura is designed to support you beyond the first moment of curiosity. This work becomes more powerful when you keep using it in real moments, especially when life gets emotional, layered, full, or uncomfortable.

