EMAIL65: RE-ENGAGEMENT EMAIL

Subject: Try this 5-minute reset if you feel weirdly off today

Hi love,

Sometimes you do not feel completely broken, but you also do not feel like yourself.

You may feel slightly disconnected, emotionally heavy, irritated, foggy, uninspired, overstimulated, or quietly tired of carrying everything. Nothing dramatic has happened, but your body feels like it is holding more than your mind has admitted.

When this happens, the instinct is often to fix everything at once.

You want a new routine, a cleaner schedule, a better plan, a deeper manifestation practice, a life reset, a nervous system reset, a new identity, and preferably a completely different emotional state by Monday morning.

But disconnection does not always need dramatic reinvention.

Sometimes it needs one honest return.

Try this 5-minute reset today:

* Place one hand on your chest and one hand on your stomach.

* Take three slow breaths without trying to change anything.

* Ask yourself, “What am I carrying right now that I have not admitted to myself?”

* Let the answer be simple and honest.

* Open Aura and bring that exact sentence to Miss Aura.

You can write:

* Help me understand why I feel this way.

* Create an EFT tapping script for this emotion.

* Give me a journaling prompt to process this.

* Help me regulate before I react from this feeling.

* Show me what belief or pattern may be underneath this.

* Guide me into a calmer state before I make any decisions.

* Help me understand whether this is anxiety, overstimulation, emotional fatigue, or an old pattern being activated.

This is what Aura was built for.

Not only the days when you feel clear, inspired, magnetic, and connected, but also the days when your mind is noisy, your body feels heavy, and your inner world needs somewhere safe to land.

Sometimes the reason we avoid returning to ourselves is not laziness. It is nervous system avoidance. Stillness can feel uncomfortable when your body is used to stimulation, urgency, or emotional survival. Aura helps you come back gently, without making your healing feel like another demand.

If it has been a while since you last used Aura, come back gently today. No guilt, no pressure, no dramatic restart. Just one honest check-in with yourself.

And if there is a reason you stopped using it, whether it was a technical issue, lack of time, confusion, payment concern, or something that did not feel smooth, please reply to this email and tell us. Your feedback genuinely helps us improve Aura, and we are always listening.

With love,
Team Aura


Data classification needed for The Aura email flow
